# How to Deploy This AWS Static Website

## 1. Prepare Your Website Files
- Make sure you have all your website files ready (`index.html`, `error.html`, `style.css`, images, etc.).
- Ensure your `index.html` file works correctly when opened locally.

## 2. Create an S3 Bucket
- Sign in to the [AWS Management Console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/s3/).
- Click on **Create Bucket**.
- Provide a unique bucket name (e.g., `my-unique-bucket-name`).
- Select a region close to you or your users.
- Leave other settings as default and click **Create bucket**.

## 3. Upload Your Website Files
- Open the bucket you just created.
- Click **Upload**, add your website files and folders.
- Click **Upload** to complete.

## 4. Configure Static Website Hosting
- In the bucket, go to the **Properties** tab.
- Scroll to **Static website hosting** and click **Edit**.
- Choose **Enable**, then select **Host a static website**.
- Set the **Index document** to `index.html`.
- Optionally specify the **Error document** as `error.html`.
- Save changes.

## 5. Make Your Bucket Content Public
- You need to allow public read access to your objects.
- Go to the **Permissions** tab in your bucket.
- Edit the **Bucket policy** to add a policy that grants public read access.
- (Policy example can be found in AWS docs.)

## 6. Access Your Static Website
- After setting up, find the **Endpoint** URL in the **Static website hosting** section.
- Open it in your browser to view your live site.
- Test your error page by navigating to a non-existent path.

